WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.730
What if you could turn the bench you already own into a complete workstation, without replacing it?

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.799
Most benches are flat surfaces with nothing above them.

00:00:12.079 --> 00:00:18.141
Tools pile on the worktop, power comes from extension boards, and there is nowhere to put bins,

00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:19.289
shelves or lights.

00:00:19.889 --> 00:00:24.636
A Link Uprighter is a heavy-gauge steel frame that mounts on top of the worktop.

00:00:24.916 --> 00:00:28.327
Its uprights are notched every inch, front and back,

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:34.492
and every Link accessory hooks into those notches: shelves, pegboards, bin rails, power rails,

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.394
lights and overhead cabinets.

00:00:36.674 --> 00:00:42.128
Move any accessory by lifting it out and re-hooking it at the same notch on both uprights.

00:00:42.728 --> 00:00:47.407
The Furnisys Link Uprighter fits Base, Scitec, Pro and packing benches,

00:00:47.407 --> 00:00:49.978
and most existing benches at your site.

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:55.267
Frames come in 30 or 48 inch heights, and 24 to 60 inch widths.

00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:58.279
So when your bench runs out of space, build up.

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:00.229
What would you hang above yours first?

00:01:00.509 --> 00:01:04.452
Comment below, and next, find out what starter and adder frames are.

00:01:05.052 --> 00:01:09.297
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

